# Every checkout, Windows included, writes text files with LF: the public export copies the working tree, and a
# CRLF NOTICE or script would be published as such. No tracked file needs CRLF (no .bat, .cmd or .ps1).
* text=auto eol=lf
# The demo assets are embedded byte for byte: a CRLF checkout would break the seed scripts.
src/connx_mcp/demo/assets/** -text
